---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const faqs = [
  ['How much does TaxDome cost?', 'TaxDome charges per seat and bills upfront: Essentials $800/seat/year (solo only), Pro $1,000/seat/year and Business $1,200/seat/year on 1-year terms, or $750, $950 and $1,150 on 2-year terms. A 3-person firm on Pro pays 3 × $1,000 = $3,000 a year, about $250 a month.'],
  ['Does TaxDome charge per client for the Bookkeeping Hub?', 'No. The Bookkeeping Hub pulls uncategorized QuickBooks Online transactions for client review with no per-client fee. Pro includes 120 ledger connections and Business includes unlimited.'],
  ['Which TaxDome alternative is cheapest for a 3-person, 20-client firm?', 'Among published prices, Financial Cents Team at 3 × $49 = $147 a month on annual billing, or $247 with the Month-End Close add-on for 20 clients. Karbon Team is 3 × $59 = $177 a month on annual billing. Double does not publish prices.'],
  ['When should a firm stay on TaxDome?', 'Stay if you also do tax work and want organizers, IRS transcripts and return delivery in the same portal, if you want clients to explain uncategorized QBO transactions without a per-client fee, or if you want a branded client portal and mobile app and are fine paying a year upfront.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="TaxDome alternatives for bookkeeping firms: practice management with published prices"
  description="Options beyond TaxDome's per-seat portal and Bookkeeping Hub: Karbon, Financial Cents and Double, with pricing verified Oct 2026 and cost for a 3-person, 20-client firm."
>
  <h1>TaxDome alternatives</h1>
  <p>TaxDome is practice management for tax and bookkeeping firms: CRM, a branded client portal and mobile app, workflows, billing and proposals, plus a Bookkeeping Hub that pulls uncategorized QuickBooks Online transactions for client review with no per-client fee. It charges per seat and bills upfront: Essentials $800/seat/year (solo only), Pro $1,000/seat/year and Business $1,200/seat/year on 1-year terms ($750, $950 and $1,150 on 2-year). Pro includes 120 ledger connections; Business includes unlimited. Firms look elsewhere when they want monthly billing, a lower seat price, shared-email triage, or month-end close on Xero as well as QBO. These are the closest options in our directory, not a full market scan.</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Alternative</th>
        <th>Best fit vs TaxDome</th>
        <th>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</th>
        <th>Trade-off</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/karbon`}>Karbon</a></td>
        <td>Teams that run client work out of shared email and want it turned into tasks, with AI email summaries, and prefer monthly billing (teams of 4+)</td>
        <td>Team $59/user/mo; Business $89/user/mo (annual); monthly $79/$99 only for teams of 4+</td>
        <td>No Bookkeeping Hub for uncategorized QBO transactions; no branded client mobile app like TaxDome</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/financial-cents`}>Financial Cents</a></td>
        <td>Solo and small QBO firms that want workflows, client chasing and billing at a lower seat price, plus an optional close add-on</td>
        <td>Solo $19/mo; Team $49/user/mo; Scale $69/user/mo (annual); Month-End Close add-on $5/client/mo</td>
        <td>Close review is a paid per-client add-on (QBO only), not included in the seat like TaxDome's Hub; lighter on tax organizers and IRS tools</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/double`}>Double</a></td>
        <td>Bookkeeping firms whose bottleneck is month-end close and client file review on QBO or Xero, not a full tax-and-bookkeeping portal</td>
        <td>Per connected client on Core, Plus, Scale and Enterprise tiers; prices not published, demo first</td>
        <td>A close and client review tool, not full practice management: no firm-wide client portal, tax organizers or time-and-billing like TaxDome</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cost for a 3-person firm with 20 clients (list prices, per month)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>TaxDome: 3 × $1,000 per year = $3,000 per year, about $250 per month (Pro), paid upfront. Pro includes the Bookkeeping Hub with 120 client ledger connections (covers 20 clients with no per-client fee).</li>
    <li>Karbon: 3 × $59 = $177 (Team, annual) or 3 × $89 = $267 (Business, annual). A 3-person team cannot pay monthly.</li>
    <li>Financial Cents: 3 × $49 = $147 (Team, annual), or $247 with the close add-on for 20 clients (20 × $5).</li>
    <li>Double: not published.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to stay on TaxDome</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You also do tax work and want organizers, IRS transcripts and return delivery in the same portal as bookkeeping.</li>
    <li>Your month-end bottleneck is getting clients to explain uncategorized QBO transactions, and you want that without paying per client.</li>
    <li>You want a branded client portal and mobile app, and you are fine paying a year upfront.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p>Sources: taxdome.com/pricing, karbonhq.com/pricing, financial-cents.com/pricing and doublehq.com/pricing checked 2026-10-18. No sponsor has paid for this comparison.</p>

  <p>
    <a href={`${b}/tools/taxdome`}>TaxDome</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/taxdome-vs-karbon`}>TaxDome vs Karbon</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/karbon-alternatives`}>Karbon alternatives</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/financial-cents-alternatives`}>Financial Cents alternatives</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/category/practice-management`}>All practice management tools</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
